item.description:
In the wake of tough midterm setbacks, the GOP faces an urgent reckoning over where its message and strategy fell short. Representative Tim Burchett (R-TN) joins The Rundown to deliver a candid autopsy of the GOP’s campaign missteps, explaining why missed opportunities on gas affordability and congressional stock trading cost them with voters. He also breaks down his push to give communities control over the boom of AI data centers, reacts to Stephen Miller stepping in as White House Chief of Staff, and discusses whether he is ready to fill Tennessee’s newly open U.S. Senate seat.&nbsp;



Is a traditional four-year degree losing its grip on the American workforce? As tuition costs climb, a deficit of skilled workers has more Americans pivoting toward trade careers. Former Pennsylvania Congressman Jason Altmire—now President and CEO of Career Education Colleges and Universities—joins the Rundown to discuss what’s driving the nationwide labor shortage, which trade jobs are most in demand, and how alternative programs train skilled workers faster and at a fraction of the cost of a university degree.

&nbsp;

PLUS, commentary by Karol Markowicz, columnist for the New York Post. 
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices

